{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created","id":1489343,"title":"So what is the oldest character you have created?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-06T09:29:36-07:00","id":1489343,"title":"So what is the oldest character you have created?","content":"For myself I barely go past the mid 18th century for any of my vampire player characters and the oldest npc I'm considering is early the early 1700's.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 08-09-2022, 02:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-06T14:26:38-07:00","id":1489365,"title":"","content":"I have a recurrent NPC that can't remember her early days, so she may be well older than that, but her oldest memories are from around the fall of Constantinople, so late 15th century. But that's for something I use more consistently, as flashbacks and whatnot sometimes do create the need for characters from earlier times.<br /> <br /> Also, you should specify that's a vampire character, as even in a Vampire game you can have characters that are other things and could be far older, specially Spirits, Demons and Fairies of any sorts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T21:35:01-07:00","id":1489450,"title":"","content":"My main character for an elders campaign was born in the mid 15th century. I think the oldest NPC I've created was from the late 18th century, though I'm not certain of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-07T23:15:26-07:00","id":1489453,"title":"","content":"Oldest character I ever played was part of a very long-duration chronicle that started during the beginnings of the Second Baali war and ended in the modern day, not too long after the destruction of Ravnos. So our characters would have been ~3,500 years old by that point.<br /> <br /> As for the oldest character at character creation, one time I was playing in a (somewhat comical) Dark Ages campaign and my character had been a vampire who'd been embraced during the Roman Republic, and then ended up getting knocked into topor just a couple of years after. He woke up like 1500 years later. I was very much playing a fish out of water character who wasn't any stronger than any other vampire PC but was suffering from massive culture shock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 08-08-2022, 02:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T07:48:33-07:00","id":1489632,"title":"","content":"Back when i was an edgy teen, my first character was a Toreador Templar from the 13th century. Probably the weakest elder to have ever existed, as i had a fledgeling character sheet. Only saving gr\u00e2ce was his 8th gen, which isn\u2019t even that good for a 13th century vampire. Oh, and i had absolutely no idea what a Toreador really was at the time, i just picked the clan because i thought Celerity was awesome and i didn\u2019t know about Brujah at the time. His art was \u2018\u2019Swordmanship\u2019\u2019. Ugh \u2026 lol.<br /> <br /> After that first mistake my PCs got younger and younger. I personally prefer playing Neonates with agenga, fighting tool and nail to gain influence and a place in the Kindred Society. I also find that the older the vampire gets, the harder it is to portray them well. There\u2019s also the issue of the number of expodential number of historical event the character has lived through as they get older.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T10:37:48-07:00","id":1489651,"title":"","content":"I have run many games outside of the default time periods so there have been lots of &quot;older&quot; characters. The oldest would be the PCs and NPCs from an all Follower of Set game set in prehistory, the PCs were all 5th gen at creation, and we played all the way to modern nights and through Gehenna. If I remember correctly, by the end all the PCs were around seven thousand years old. As such the only entities that could be much of a challenge would be even older things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T16:46:36-07:00","id":1489689,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created?p=1489632#post1489632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back when i was an edgy teen, my first character was a Toreador Templar from the 13th century. Probably the weakest elder to have ever existed, as i had a fledgeling character sheet. Only saving gr\u00e2ce was his 8th gen, which isn\u2019t even that good for a 13th century vampire. Oh, and i had absolutely no idea what a Toreador really was at the time, i just picked the clan because i thought Celerity was awesome and i didn\u2019t know about Brujah at the time. His art was \u2018\u2019Swordmanship\u2019\u2019. Ugh \u2026 lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>First character, a ST apparently with little to no idea of setting's expectations to nudge the player into a more fitting concept either, it happens.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created?p=1489632#post1489632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After that first mistake my PCs got younger and younger. I personally prefer playing Neonates with agenga, fighting tool and nail to gain influence and a place in the Kindred Society. I also find that the older the vampire gets, the harder it is to portray them well. There\u2019s also the issue of the number of expodential number of historical event the character has lived through as they get older.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me it depends on occasion, sometimes will go with a quite fresh neonate, others with a fish out of water walking anachronism of recently awakened from torpor vampire, going from anything between hippy from the 60s to a &quot;nubian&quot; from sometime between 16th-3rd century BC, who would find itself amidst the collection of &quot;egyptian relics&quot; of a millionaire that would be the PC's first victim upon awakening.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 08-10-2022, 07:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T06:40:33-07:00","id":1489739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created?p=1489689#post1489689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First character, a ST apparently with little to no idea of setting's expectations to nudge the player into a more fitting concept either, it happens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, to be fair, my ST was around my age at the time, so we were truly just a bunch of teenagers larping in a setting we barely understood. We still had fun at the time and that's what count! I just cringe a tiny bit when i look back at my first character concepts. I'm not ahasmed though, it's the good kind of cringe, if such a thing exist. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created?p=1489689#post1489689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For me it depends on occasion, sometimes will go with a quite fresh neonate, others with a fish out of water walking anachronism of recently awakened from torpor vampire, going from anything between hippy from the 60s to a &quot;nubian&quot; from sometime between 16th-3rd century BC, who would find itself amidst the collection of &quot;egyptian relics&quot; of a millionaire that would be the PC's first victim upon awakening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah the ol ''Ancient that just awaken'' is an interesting concept as they have to relearn basically everything about society. I find that such character make excellent critics of today's standard of society as they look at it from a different lense. I'm not opposed to playing elders, i just find them hard to portray well, especially if they have been active. I personally take my character's backstory rather seriously and Elders are just a pain to write up for me most of the time. However, they do give me an excuse to take the time to research historical events, so there's that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-11T20:50:37-07:00","id":1489833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created?p=1489739#post1489739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, to be fair, my ST was around my age at the time, so we were truly just a bunch of teenagers larping in a setting we barely understood. We still had fun at the time and that's what count! I just cringe a tiny bit when i look back at my first character concepts. I'm not ahasmed though, it's the good kind of cringe, if such a thing exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, having fun at the expense some of our own past moments is certainly part of life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489343-so-what-is-the-oldest-character-you-have-created?p=1489739#post1489739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah the ol ''Ancient that just awaken'' is an interesting concept as they have to relearn basically everything about society. I find that such character make excellent critics of today's standard of society as they look at it from a different lense. I'm not opposed to playing elders, i just find them hard to portray well, especially if they have been active. I personally take my character's backstory rather seriously and Elders are just a pain to write up for me most of the time. However, they do give me an excuse to take the time to research historical events, so there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a concept with the convenience of being easily reworked depending on clan, era &amp; a bunch of other details plus being mostly simple to insert in a basic starting table and/or with a new group. Elder characters require a ST in the mood for certain power levels <b>and</b> trusting the players with them from the get go.<br /> <br /> Now speaking of character with the <i>longest <b>active </b></i>unlife, that would be a coin toss between Mirkal, a Caitiff who, depending on who's telling the tale based on dubious sources and his own serial diablerie-messed memories, is either an apprentice of Goratrix who was embraced and went rogue amidst a botched early attempt at creating the Gargoyles, or a pre-teen magician who was part of a blood cult in the hellenistic period whose attempt to master the secrets of their mysterious blood gods went terribly awry or Akirev, a terible revenge-fueled maniac dedicated to anihilating the monsters who ruined the home city and people from his mortal years - though it's possible even he doesn't know anymore if his nemeses/makers were Baali, Cappadocian, Salubri, Setites or more probably something garbled, mixed and wicked inbetween long confused in the mists of time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 09-22-2022, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T09:13:13-07:00","id":1489890,"title":"","content":"Ancient Mesopotamia Baali. Long campaign about demons. <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">3100 BCE</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27541-heavywhiskey","name":"HeavyWhiskey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27541_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:41:20-07:00","id":1489961,"title":"","content":"We did a crazy short campign once where we were the neonates in the Second City an were tol by our sires to flee just a the city w going down. We fled westwards and found places to sleep in. Then we woke up in 2002 in UK and it ws hillarious to play Kindred of the 5th generation that had slept or thousands and thousands years and had to deal with understanding modern times","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>This space for rent.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25995-ethryo","name":"Ethryo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"67"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-12T15:54:51-07:00","id":1489963,"title":"","content":"4th gen, 5.000 BC bronze age, second city","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-16T10:47:31-07:00","id":1490405,"title":"","content":"4th gen first childe of Absimiliard (non-canon). So First City pre-flood. A male Cleopatra.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-18T18:50:27-07:00","id":1490669,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty much always the GM, and I homebrew everything (including the origins of vampirism) so the oldest character I've actually statted is the oldest surviving vampire in my world -- a Gangrel named Dilgan. He is the first childe of the first childe of the first vampire (the Gangrel clan Founder, who kicked it in 300 AD). He's approximately 3,961 years old. Here's his capsule write-up:<br /> <br /> <i>Dilgan was a Priest in Lagash, a man of profound wisdom and bearing who was embraced by Aeliameh to be her companion (in much the same way that Namtar embraced her). This coupling, however, was far more successful, though their relationship was never romantic in nature. Rather, they were the very best of true \u201cfriends\u201d, if such a term does not sound out of place among vampires. When Aeliameh left for Persia, Dilgan initially stayed behind, although he took a 300-year hiatus to go visit her at one point, residing in and around Estakhr from around 120-420 AD. He returned to Mosul around 420, however, confident that his sire would return and wanting to prepare her way. Dilgan is almost certainly the oldest living vampire in the world, having been the fifth vampire ever created. He is profoundly weighed down with Stigmata, suffering from no fewer than a seventeen of them. Nevertheless, he has maintained his humanity remarkably well considering the circumstances, and still feels passion and yearning and loss in a way that many five-hundred-year olds have already lost. He has three times embraced a woman with whom he was \u201cin love\u201d and all three times it has ended badly. He has sworn not to create any further vampires and is one of the most vocal proponents of the Third Tradition being strictly enforced. He does not consider vampirism a gift but sees it as a curse that can and should ultimately be borne. He has great hatred in his heart for the Sabbat, seeing in them the ruination of the human world and the death of his beloved sire, with whom he spent over 2,000 years. Dilgan is known among truly ancient vampires as \u201cThe Divine Star\u201d \u2013 but it is not a name that would be known to anyone born after the death of the Christ.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13136-legendre","name":"Legendre","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13136_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"328"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T07:03:05-07:00","id":1490708,"title":"","content":"In a one shot, we played as Antediluvians (I was Tzimisce), we had Brujah, Arikel, Malkav and Haquim. You can imagine where it did go when we embraced for the first time ^^<br /> In a more developped chronicle (Black Cross, but prolonged to modern time with demonic possession in the background), I made a 7th gen True Brujah librarian (the kind that save knowledge from undeserving people) born in 999.<br /> In my group, we tend to do chronicles of ages stuff. Mostly beginning in dark ages or before, and trying to survive until present time.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7454-darthpalpy","name":"Darthpalpy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7454_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"77"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-14T16:30:17-07:00","id":1493080,"title":"","content":"Well, it was an NPC, and he\u2019s never once appeared \u201con-camera\u201d, but I had a ridiculously old 5th-Generation Cappadocian. We\u2019re talking Ancient Akkad. He has been the villain behind all my oWoD games, and my players have no idea. This has been going on for over a decade. Granted, in modern games he\u2019s a Harbinger of Skulls, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-16T10:19:51-07:00","id":1493168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong